Command: authenticated Puppeteer capture of /config at 1440x900, 768x1024, and 390x844
Exit status: visual QA failed

Observed failure:
- GET /system/admin-health returned one card per failed customer email.
- The seeded database contained 7,709 failed emails, so pagination returned 100 email cards.
- Setup, users/permissions, configuration, database, durable delivery jobs, and audit sources were starved from the first page.
- The endpoint was truthful but did not provide the source-level system-management overview required by the Admin workspace.

Root cause:
- adminHealth() expanded durable_effect_jobs and customer_email_logs rows individually instead of aggregating each health source.

Fix:
- Aggregate failed durable jobs and failed customer emails into one source card each.
- Retain the real failure count and latest source freshness.
- Emit a healthy zero-failure source card when the query succeeds with no failed rows.
- Keep query failure mapped to UNAVAILABLE; never infer HEALTHY from an unavailable source.

Re-run evidence is recorded in qa/2026-08-22_role-workspaces_wave3_manual.log.
